## Report

### Files created
- `/home/v0id/Documents/repos/residual/web/src/main.ts` — new orchestration entry point.
- `/home/v0id/Documents/repos/residual/scripts/gen-view-bundle.sh` — bundle build script (executable).
- `/home/v0id/Documents/repos/residual/web/generated/app.js` — checked-in compiled bundle (57KB, 12 modules, fully self-contained: `grep -c "^import "` / `require(` = 0).

### Files edited
- `/home/v0id/Documents/repos/residual/src/view/shell.html`
- `/home/v0id/Documents/repos/residual/src/view/static_export.rs`
- `/home/v0id/Documents/repos/residual/src/view/mod.rs`

### Files deleted
- `/home/v0id/Documents/repos/residual/src/view/commands.rs` (confirmed no other references to `commands::`/`StagedAdd`/`format_add_command(s)` anywhere in `src/` before deleting).

### `main.ts` (full content)
```ts
import { snapshotToPendingState, type RawLandscapeSnapshot } from "./snapshot-bridge";
import { mount as mountMatrix } from "./matrix-interactions";
import { mountForms, regenerateStagedCommands } from "./forms";
import { mountImportModal } from "./import-modal";
import { mountExportScript } from "./export-script";
import type { PendingState } from "./model";

const snapshotElement = document.getElementById("residual-snapshot");
const rawSnapshot: RawLandscapeSnapshot = snapshotElement
  ? (JSON.parse(snapshotElement.textContent ?? "{}") as RawLandscapeSnapshot)
  : { attractors: [], stressors: [], purposes: [], components: [], residues: [] };

let state: PendingState = snapshotToPendingState(rawSnapshot);
const getState = (): PendingState => state;
const setState = (next: PendingState): void => { state = next; };

const container = document.querySelector("main") ?? document.body;
const table = container.querySelector<HTMLTableElement>("table.matrix");

if (table) {
  const matrixMount = mountMatrix(table, getState, setState, {
    onChange: () => {
      regenerateStagedCommands(container as HTMLElement, getState);
      matrixMount.syncNewRows();
    },
  });

  const onChange = (): void => {
    regenerateStagedCommands(container as HTMLElement, getState);
    matrixMount.syncNewRows();
  };

  mountForms(container as HTMLElement, getState, setState, { onChange });
  mountImportModal(container as HTMLElement, getState, setState, { onChange });
  mountExportScript(container as HTMLElement, getState, { onChange });
}

regenerateStagedCommands(container as HTMLElement, getState);
```
No `DOMContentLoaded` wrapper — confirmed the script is placed at the very end of `<body>` after `<main>` and the snapshot `<script>`, matching the old inline pattern.

### shell.html additions
- Toolbar: `<label><input type="checkbox" data-show-proposed-toggle checked /> show proposed</label>` and matching `data-show-unrelated-toggle` (both default `checked`, per `forms.test.ts`'s fixture).
- `<p data-component-form-error></p>` immediately after the `data-command-generator="component"` form.
- In the copy-bar: `<button type="button" data-generate-script>generate bash script</button>` and `<button type="button" data-import-trigger>import</button>`.
- New import-modal block (matches `import-modal.ts`'s documented contract exactly):
```html
<div class="import-modal" data-import-modal hidden>
  <h2>Import staged commands</h2>
  <p class="import-modal-hint">Paste <code>residual add …</code> / <code>residual update …</code> lines below.</p>
  <label>commands</label>
  <textarea data-import-primary placeholder="residual add stressor --description …"></textarea>
  <label>lines that failed to parse</label>
  <textarea data-import-errors readonly placeholder="unparsed lines appear here"></textarea>
  <ul data-import-error-list class="import-error-list"></ul>
  <div class="copy-bar">
    <button type="button" data-import-run>import</button>
    <button type="button" data-import-retry>retry</button>
  </div>
</div>
```
- Deleted the entire old inline `<script>…</script>` block (`shellQuote`/`pushFlag`/`buildAddCommand`/filter/sort/accordion/fusion-fission JS), kept the `<script id="residual-snapshot" …>` block, and added `<script type="module">{{APP_JS}}</script>` right after it.

### CSS added
```css
--danger: #e6453e;
...
th.sticky-col.row-invalid,
tr.force-row.row-invalid,
tr.force-row.row-invalid td,
th[data-component].row-invalid {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--danger) 30%, transparent);
  outline: 2px solid var(--danger);
  outline-offset: -2px;
}
[role="menu"] { position: absolute; z-index: 50; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0.25rem; min-width: 10rem; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.4); }
[role="menuitem"] { padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem; font: 12px/1.3 var(--mono); color: var(--ink); cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; }
[role="menuitem"]:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, transparent); color: var(--accent); }
.import-modal { margin-top: 0.75rem; padding: 1rem 1.1rem 1.15rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface) 92%, black); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
.import-modal[hidden] { display: none; }
.import-modal-hint { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
.import-error-list { margin: 0 0 0.55rem; padding-left: 1.1rem; color: var(--warn); font: 12px/1.4 var(--mono); }
```

### static_export.rs changes
- Added `APP_JS_PLACEHOLDER = "{{APP_JS}}"` and `APP_JS: &str = include_str!("../../web/generated/app.js")`, wired into `render_landscape_html`'s `.replace(...)` chain.
- Fixed forward 3 tests whose assertions checked for now-nonexistent inline JS functions/strings (`buildAddCommand`, `shellQuote`, contiguous `--flag` substrings — confirmed empirically these don't appear as contiguous literals in the bundle since `model.ts` builds them via `` `--${name}` `` template interpolation): `html_contains_command_generator_and_copy_surface`, `template_asset_carries_placeholder_and_generator_js`.
- Trimmed `template_wires_live_fusion_fission_threshold` to markup-only assertions (`data-fusion-fission-filter`, `data-threshold-input`), dropping the dead JS-function assertions.
- **Deleted** `template_wires_working_filter_js_to_matrix_rows`, `template_wires_click_to_sort_on_matrix_headers`, `template_wires_force_accordion_toggle` outright — their markup-level assertions were already redundant with other still-passing tests (`html_matrix_rows_carry_filterable_force_data`, `html_matrix_headers_carry_sort_and_status_metadata`, `html_force_rows_are_accordions_labeled_by_shortname`), and their only unique content was asserting inline JS that no longer exists anywhere.
- Added a new test, `template_and_html_embed_the_compiled_app_bundle`, asserting the `{{APP_JS}}` placeholder exists in `TEMPLATE`, `APP_JS` is non-empty, and rendered output embeds a `<script type="module">` with the placeholder fully substituted.
- `html_command_generator_does_not_mutate_the_ledger` needed no changes — verified empirically the bundle contains zero occurrences of `fetch(`, `XMLHttpRequest`, `navigator.sendBeacon`.

### Important deviation — please review

**Filter box, click-to-sort column headers, accordion-toggle expand/collapse, and the live fusion/fission threshold slider no longer work.** These were implemented entirely in the old inline `<script>` and are not reimplemented anywhere in the tested `web/src/*.ts` modules (confirmed by grep — no TS file outside `*.test.ts` references `data-force-filter`, `sortMatrixBy`, `data-accordion-toggle` wiring, or `thresholdInput`). The task's explicit instructions were to delete that script wholesale and fix forward any now-stale tests (naming `shellQuote` as an example), and `main.ts` was explicitly scoped to "no new business logic, no DOM manipulation beyond wiring" — so I did not attempt to patch this gap myself, since doing so would mean either violating the "don't touch other `web/src/*.ts` files" constraint or adding real DOM logic to `main.ts` against its explicit scope. I flagged this via a doc-comment on the surviving `template_wires_live_fusion_fission_threshold` test and in this report rather than silently absorbing the regression. This looks like it needs a follow-up phase to reimplement filter/sort/accordion-toggle/threshold logic in a proper TS module (e.g. a new `matrix-view.ts` or extending `render-decisions.ts`).

### Verification (Step 7)
1. `cd web && bun test` (ad-hoc `nix shell nixpkgs#bun`, since `nix develop` couldn't enter before `app.js` existed) — **169 pass, 0 fail**, 704 expect() calls.
2. `nix shell nixpkgs#cargo nixpkgs#rustc nixpkgs#gcc -c cargo test` — **all green** (309 unit tests + 4 + 5 + 30 integration tests, 0 failures).
3. `nix develop -c cargo test` (flake/crane sandboxed check-phase, after `git add -A` staged the new files) — **all green**, same counts.
4. `nix develop -c residual verify all` — `OK: all checks passed.`
5. `nix develop -c cargo clippy --all-targets -- --deny warnings` — confirmed via `git stash`/`clippy`/`git stash pop` that the two warnings appearing in `static_export.rs` (`SNAPSHOT_ELEMENT_ID`/`extract_snapshot_json` "never used") are **pre-existing**, unrelated to this change (identical on the pre-change tree). `mod.rs` and my new test produce zero clippy findings.
6. Manual smoke test: `nix develop -c residual view --out /tmp/residual-view-smoke` → `landscape.html`. Confirmed: `<script type="module">` present with 57,109 chars of bundled JS; zero unresolved `{{...}}` placeholders; `data-show-proposed-toggle`, `data-import-trigger`, `data-generate-script`, `data-component-form-error` all present. Temp dir removed after the check.

No red tests, no broken build — the one outstanding item is the filter/sort/accordion/threshold functionality gap documented above, which I'm surfacing rather than silently declaring fully done.
